      "text": "To find the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285, we need to determine the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 342 and 285. Let's start by finding the prime factorizations of both numbers.\n\nFirst, we factorize 342:\n\\[ 342 \\div 2 = 171 \\]\n\\[ 171 \\div 3 = 57 \\]\n\\[ 57 \\div 3 = 19 \\]\n\\[ 19 \\div 19 = 1 \\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 342 is:\n\\[ 342 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 19 \\]\n\nNext, we factorize 285:\n\\[ 285 \\div 3 = 95 \\]\n\\[ 95 \\div 5 = 19 \\]\n\\[ 19 \\div 19 = 1 \\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 285 is:\n\\[ 285 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 19 \\]\n\nNow, we identify the common prime factors of 342 and 285. The common prime factors are 3 and 19. The lowest power of 3 that appears in both factorizations is \\(3^1\\), and the lowest power of 19 that appears in both factorizations is \\(19^1\\). Therefore, the GCD is:\n\\[ \\text{GCD}(342, 285) = 3 \\times 19 = 57 \\]\n\nThus, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is \\(\\boxed{57}\\).",
