      "text": "To find the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285, we need to determine the greatest common divisor (GCD) of the two numbers. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Find the prime factorizations of 342 and 285**:\n   - First, factorize 342:\n     \\[\n     342 \\div 2 = 171 \\quad \\text{(so, 2 is a factor)}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     171 \\div 3 = 57 \\quad \\text{(so, 3 is a factor)}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     57 \\div 3 = 19 \\quad \\text{(so, 3 is a factor again)}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     19 \\quad \\text{is a prime number, so, 19 is a factor}\n     \\]\n     Therefore, the prime factorization of 342 is:\n     \\[\n     342 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 19\n     \\]\n\n   - Now factorize 285:\n     \\[\n     285 \\div 3 = 95 \\quad \\text{(so, 3 is a factor)}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     95 \\div 5 = 19 \\quad \\text{(so, 5 is a factor)}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     19 \\quad \\text{is a prime number, so, 19 is a factor}\n     \\]\n     Therefore, the prime factorization of 285 is:\n     \\[\n     285 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 19\n     \\]\n\n2. **Determine the GCD by finding the common prime factors**:\n   - The common prime factors of 342 and 285 are 3, 5, and 19.\n   - The lowest power of these common prime factors is \\(3^1\\), \\(5^1\\), and \\(19^1\\).\n   - Therefore, the GCD of 342 and 285 is:\n     \\[\n     3 \\times 5 \\times 19 = 285\n     \\]\n\n3. **Conclusion**:\n   - The largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is the GCD of 342 and 285, which is 285.\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{285}\n\\]",
