      "text": "The prime factorization of 342 is $2\\cdot3^2\\cdot19$. The prime factorization of 285 is $3\\cdot5\\cdot19$.\n\nTo find the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285, we need to find the greatest common divisor (gcd) of 342 and 285.\n\nThe gcd of two numbers is the largest positive integer that divides both numbers without leaving a remainder. We can find the gcd by determining the common prime factors of the two numbers and taking the lowest power of each prime that appears in both factorizations.\n\nThe common prime factors of 342 and 285 are 3 and 19. The lowest power of 3 common to both factorizations is $3^1$ and the lowest power of 19 common to both factorizations is $19^1$.\n\nTherefore, the gcd of 342 and 285 is $3^1\\cdot19^1 = 3\\cdot19 = \\boxed{57}$.The answer is: 57",
